{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons","id":11982,"title":"Can Angels be nearly as complex and cool as Demons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-16T03:18:50-08:00","id":11982,"title":"Can Angels be nearly as complex and cool as Demons?","content":"Okay I haven't read all the stuff on Demons and Angels, but Angels are built like Spirits and Ghosts, while Demons have all these cool complex powers. But Demons are fallen angels. Can angels as NPCs be built to have nearly as much cool &quot;stuff&quot; as Demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T04:34:08-08:00","id":11996,"title":"","content":"If you really USE the influences that angels have I would say they can easily be as cool there effectwise (and even be more powerful there).<br /> <br /> (From what I have seen most don't really put influences,... to real use, and instead use them only very very directly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T05:11:08-08:00","id":12001,"title":"","content":"If you're asking &quot;can I make something with as many mechanical options as the Unchained,&quot; that depends on how experienced a demon you're talking about versus the angel's Rank.<br /> <br /> If you're asking &quot;can I make a compelling and complex character out of an angel,&quot; then the answer is absolutely. I run several different games that are all in the same continuity (so that characters in one city can hear about what happened in another city and so forth), and my one recurring NPC is an angel of sorts. (I don't want to say too much in case my players take a look at this.) For most of that NPC's existence - and certainly throughout our Demon playtest games - she was a normal angel. I didn't fully realize what type of angel she was until I played her a bit. And she's the one NPC that my players who play in more than one group see show up and immediately groan, knowing what sort of trouble is about to unfold. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T06:20:47-08:00","id":12026,"title":"","content":"Not really. Angels as presented don't really have much going on in the way of personality to speak of, so it seems to me that most of your most interesting angels would be ones on the brink of falling anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T08:04:29-08:00","id":12075,"title":"","content":"I don't know about that, I think Angels can have complex personalities. I mean look at Agent Smith in The Matrix, he was pretty complex there, I feel he became more on exile in the second and third however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T09:05:11-08:00","id":12102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=12075#post12075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about that, I think Angels can have complex personalities. I mean look at Agent Smith in The Matrix, he was pretty complex there, I feel he became more on exile in the second and third however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about Smith, and really he's the only Agent in the movie with much of a personality, and in the end he winds up becoming a rogue element, with a pretty strong analog to falling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:17:55-08:00","id":12353,"title":"","content":"I think his style suits Exile slightly better - he's not hunted by the Machines in quite the same way as a Fallen-analogue would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T17:36:47-08:00","id":12395,"title":"","content":"He is hunted though, the problem is he outclasses his persuers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T19:43:15-08:00","id":12451,"title":"","content":"Much like other splats, end game for Demon likely means outclassing the opposition at last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T07:37:55-08:00","id":12718,"title":"","content":"He falls because Neo ... something something code overwritten something -ed him, though (the green explosion move at the end.) He had a unique, memorable personality throughout the original film, without Falling at all.<br /> <br /> With that said, he was clearly something of a loose cannon, as Agents go. Even before he turned into an unstoppable virus and overwrote his former colleagues, the other programs in the Matrix, passers-by ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:21:11-08:00","id":13480,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one that gets a bit of an inconsistent thematic from Angels?<br /> <br /> They are supposed to be the ever-present threat to Demons. Slip up with your cover, do something obvious, get flagged and the hunter/killer Angel's will descend and you are boned. <br /> <br /> Yet in the infrastructure section it really stresses how hard it is to bring an Angel out of stasis and how much harder then that it is to make a new Angel. In another part of Chapter 1 its mentioned several times that Angel's spend the vast majority of their immortal existence in stasis, only brought out of such a state for specific task (via infrastructure). So it's kinda hard to see them being an ever present threat. <br /> <br /> This dissidence can be reconciled by an ST deciding that at any one time there are a lot more Angel's around the world then there are Unchained. Yet I don't think that's really all that implied in the core book. Likewise, its kinda a necessary conceit if you are going to explain how an Angel can always get to a compromised Demon in a short enough time that its going to be a problem for any Unchained without a backup or burn cover. <br /> <br /> Also the actual threat Angel's present is a bit inconsistent in the book. Sometimes they are presented and talked about as much more powerful, with abilities that Demons can only ape and raw power that even a Demon &quot;going loud&quot; can only just reach. Yet in other sections Demons take on multiple Angels at once and either win or force them to retreat. Which is a bit weird. I always got the impression that fighting an Angel was always a bad idea. Most of the time its more powerful then you and even if its not there is no point destroying it because there are always more on their way as long as the GM can find you e.g. being in Demonic Form. <br /> <br /> The second point feeds back into my first point. If Angels are actually pretty rare in the world and hard to even get out of stasis then fighting and destroying enough of them might be a legitimate tactic, as the GM may temporally &quot;run out&quot; of Angels in your immediate area (city). Fighting goes from being a last ditch tactic to a plausible plan to deal with the GM in the area. Which I don't feel fits with the &quot;enemy agent behind enemy lines&quot; feel of Demon. <br /> <br /> As a third point. How immortal are Angels? We know they don't age and don't need to eat, sleep and are immune to poisons and disease. Yet if a Demon destroy's an angel with physical might and supernatural power is the Angel dead? As this once again runs into the problem of the &quot;hard to create new Angels&quot; fluff. Demons could likely destroy more Angels then the GM could produce if a large Agency in an area made a push at it. Which once again seems to undermine the themes of Demon quite a bit. <br /> <br /> I guess my own thematic dissidence over this point springs from a preconception I have. After reading the Demon Quickstarter I very much characterized angels like the Agents of the Matrix films. They are stronger and faster then you. They have access to senses and information beyond you. They exist as a &quot;core&quot; of programming and essence. They inhabit the form they do for efficiency's stake. If you fight one, you might win through luck or skill or lateral thinking, but at best its a temporary respite. They will be back and the best you can do is inconvenience them long enough to escape and hide again. Demon's meanwhile are &quot;mortal&quot; trapped in the forms they fell in and trapped in the last cover they had. Their transient but immortal selves cut off from the God Machine making them mortal. Much like the exiled programs in the later Matrix films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T16:02:44-08:00","id":13669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=12718#post12718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He falls because Neo ... something something code overwritten something -ed him, though (the green explosion move at the end.) He had a unique, memorable personality throughout the original film, without Falling at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of overwritten codes seems to be the basis for how they have a connection, and possibly Smith's new superpower, but it seems more likely that his obsession was the basis of him being compelled to stay and to disobey.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T17:45:12-08:00","id":13710,"title":"","content":"I've been considering similar things Hawthorn, and one of the ideas that's struck me include things like the Clockwork &amp; Dalga from the GMC book, amongst others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:53:00-08:00","id":13762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=13480#post13480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one that gets a bit of an inconsistent thematic from Angels?<br /> <br /> They are supposed to be the ever-present threat to Demons. Slip up with your cover, do something obvious, get flagged and the hunter/killer Angel's will descend and you are boned.<br /> <br /> Yet in the infrastructure section it really stresses how hard it is to bring an Angel out of stasis and how much harder then that it is to make a new Angel. In another part of Chapter 1 its mentioned several times that Angel's spend the vast majority of their immortal existence in stasis, only brought out of such a state for specific task (via infrastructure). So it's kinda hard to see them being an ever present threat.<br /> <br /> This dissidence can be reconciled by an ST deciding that at any one time there are a lot more Angel's around the world then there are Unchained. Yet I don't think that's really all that implied in the core book. Likewise, its kinda a necessary conceit if you are going to explain how an Angel can always get to a compromised Demon in a short enough time that its going to be a problem for any Unchained without a backup or burn cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels aren't the only servants of the God-Machine, though. If an angel isn't available for whatever reason (there isn't Infrastructure in place to provide any requisite Condition for that sort of angel to appear, for instance), then cultists can also work. I mean, a demon might be able to cut through mortals like crazy...or the demon might get pinned down with gunfire. Or maybe some of the cultists actually possess some supernatural powers themselves, in the form of the Supernatural Merits from GMC.<br /> <br /> Angels are certainly the most powerful enemies of the Unchained (by and large), but they aren't the only tool in the God-Machine's toolbox. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=13480#post13480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the actual threat Angel's present is a bit inconsistent in the book. Sometimes they are presented and talked about as much more powerful, with abilities that Demons can only ape and raw power that even a Demon &quot;going loud&quot; can only just reach. Yet in other sections Demons take on multiple Angels at once and either win or force them to retreat. Which is a bit weird. I always got the impression that fighting an Angel was always a bad idea. Most of the time its more powerful then you and even if its not there is no point destroying it because there are always more on their way as long as the GM can find you e.g. being in Demonic Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that may be tied, mechanically speaking, to Rank. Obviously, lower-Ranked angels would be easier to defeat than their more powerful counterparts. Of course it also depends on how experienced the demon is as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=13480#post13480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second point feeds back into my first point. If Angels are actually pretty rare in the world and hard to even get out of stasis then fighting and destroying enough of them might be a legitimate tactic, as the GM may temporally &quot;run out&quot; of Angels in your immediate area (city). Fighting goes from being a last ditch tactic to a plausible plan to deal with the GM in the area. Which I don't feel fits with the &quot;enemy agent behind enemy lines&quot; feel of Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual combat part might not (although demons can be rather scary in combat, I've found), but they'd need to discover all of the intel needed to conclude that destroying angels in a particular area is a feasible plan. That definitely fits into the game quite well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=13480#post13480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a third point. How immortal are Angels? We know they don't age and don't need to eat, sleep and are immune to poisons and disease. Yet if a Demon destroy's an angel with physical might and supernatural power is the Angel dead? As this once again runs into the problem of the &quot;hard to create new Angels&quot; fluff. Demons could likely destroy more Angels then the GM could produce if a large Agency in an area made a push at it. Which once again seems to undermine the themes of Demon quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>As best I can tell, angels are as immortal as a given Storyteller wants them to be.<br /> <br /> As far as the rest of that paragraph - what story arises from that? If the PC's can destroy all of the angels in an area, what happens then? Do they create their own pocket Hell? Conversely, what happens if they destroy all of the angels, and the city starts breaking down into uncontrolled anarchy because some of those angels were needed to keep certain aspects of the city working properly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=13480#post13480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my own thematic dissidence over this point springs from a preconception I have. After reading the Demon Quickstarter I very much characterized angels like the Agents of the Matrix films. They are stronger and faster then you. They have access to senses and information beyond you. They exist as a &quot;core&quot; of programming and essence. They inhabit the form they do for efficiency's stake. If you fight one, you might win through luck or skill or lateral thinking, but at best its a temporary respite. They will be back and the best you can do is inconvenience them long enough to escape and hide again. Demon's meanwhile are &quot;mortal&quot; trapped in the forms they fell in and trapped in the last cover they had. Their transient but immortal selves cut off from the God Machine making them mortal. Much like the exiled programs in the later Matrix films.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's not far off. I only got to run one &quot;real&quot; combat when I've run Demon, and it really could have gone either way. Only some quick thinking from the players and a few lucky rolls really swung the combat with angels in their direction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T21:09:52-08:00","id":13774,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=13480#post13480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a third point. How immortal are Angels? We know they don't age and don't need to eat, sleep and are immune to poisons and disease. Yet if a Demon destroy's an angel with physical might and supernatural power is the Angel dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Ephemeral entities that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated wounds explode into a burst of ephemera stylized to their nature. A forest-spirit dies in a hail of rapidly-vanishing pine needles, while ghosts crumble, screaming, into the ground. The entity isn\u2019t actually dead, though, unless it has also run out of Essence. If it has even a single Essence point remaining, it reforms in a safe place (a Conditioned location, usually), hibernating.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T02:27:11-08:00","id":13886,"title":"","content":"You can always use embeds or exploits described as Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T07:17:35-08:00","id":14020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=13774#post13774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Ephemeral entities that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated wounds explode into a burst of ephemera stylized to their nature. A forest-spirit dies in a hail of rapidly-vanishing pine needles, while ghosts crumble, screaming, into the ground. The entity isn\u2019t actually dead, though, unless it has also run out of Essence. If it has even a single Essence point remaining, it reforms in a safe place (a Conditioned location, usually), hibernating.&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I've been so caught up in all the new Demon rules stuff (plus running Mummy) that I completely forgot about the GMC's core rules for ephemeral entities. Duh. This does address the &quot;immortality&quot; question pretty well. Likewise, it stops the &quot;kill all Angels tactic&quot; from being so viable. As you would have to destroy all Infrastructure as well in short order (before they the Angel's came back out of stasis) to make sure the Angel's did not come back. Which is the sort of thing that might make for an interesting &quot;final act&quot; in a Demon campaign. <br /> <br /> To address some of Strider's points - <br /> <br /> True enough on the issue of other possible adversaries. I just got a strong feeling of &quot;cannon fodder&quot; from a lot of the Cultist stuff. This does not mean they can't be dangerous in a number of different ways. I like the idea of a subversion where a cult leader is actually the big-bad or massively dangerous due to his contacts and/or intellect.<br /> <br /> Rank is the obvious explanation. I guess, once again this falls to the ST to manage really. If the ST wants his Angels to always be more powerful then the Demons involved in the Campaign I guess he makes them Rank 4 and 5. If he wants some Angels to just be dogsbodies he makes a few Rank 2 and 3 ones that are getting on with tasks that require less raw power then hunting the Unchained might. <br /> <br /> The point that Satchel raised kinda addresses the &quot;run out of Angels&quot; problem I mentioned. I agree that the info gathering part (trying to find out how many Angel's there are active in a city at any given time) is very in theme for Demon. Linked to this I do like the idea that Demons (except maybe Saboteurs) don't try to do maximum damage to the God Machine because they are afraid of the consequences that may have on the world. A city starts to crumble, or the laws of physics start screwing up, time starts to malfunction, things worse then the agents of the God Machine starts to leak into the world and become a new major problem for the Unchained. <br /> <br /> All good stuff.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think the majority of my thematic concerns have been addressed. The rules I had forgotten, plus the level of customization an ST can have on Angels means that they function well in the role I presupposed they did by default, but also work in other thematic placements as well e.g. weaker Angels that can be destroyed. Plus I really like the idea of the consequences for the world if Angels and Infrastructure stopped being present. <br /> <br /> \u200bThanks guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T08:31:16-08:00","id":14070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=14020#post14020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough on the issue of other possible adversaries. I just got a strong feeling of &quot;cannon fodder&quot; from a lot of the Cultist stuff. This does not mean they can't be dangerous in a number of different ways. I like the idea of a subversion where a cult leader is actually the big-bad or massively dangerous due to his contacts and/or intellect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it depends on what Embeds your PC's have, I suppose. My first session, I failed to remember that one of the PC's had Cool Heads Prevail, and that just stopped the fight cold before it even started. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=14020#post14020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank is the obvious explanation. I guess, once again this falls to the ST to manage really. If the ST wants his Angels to always be more powerful then the Demons involved in the Campaign I guess he makes them Rank 4 and 5. If he wants some Angels to just be dogsbodies he makes a few Rank 2 and 3 ones that are getting on with tasks that require less raw power then hunting the Unchained might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=14020#post14020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point that Satchel raised kinda addresses the &quot;run out of Angels&quot; problem I mentioned. I agree that the info gathering part (trying to find out how many Angel's there are active in a city at any given time) is very in theme for Demon. Linked to this I do like the idea that Demons (except maybe Saboteurs) don't try to do maximum damage to the God Machine because they are afraid of the consequences that may have on the world. A city starts to crumble, or the laws of physics start screwing up, time starts to malfunction, things worse then the agents of the God Machine starts to leak into the world and become a new major problem for the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if it fits the story, maybe the God-Machine decides that, hey, there is a very large thorn in its proverbial paw (i.e. the PC's) and decides to start working on Infrastructure that will summon a very powerful (Rank 6+) angel to wipe them - and the city - off the map. That could drive an entire story in its own right as the PC's try to figure out the occult matrix and stop it before their own very personal doomsday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11982-can-angels-be-nearly-as-complex-and-cool-as-demons?p=14020#post14020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I think the majority of my thematic concerns have been addressed. The rules I had forgotten, plus the level of customization an ST can have on Angels means that they function well in the role I presupposed they did by default, but also work in other thematic placements as well e.g. weaker Angels that can be destroyed. Plus I really like the idea of the consequences for the world if Angels and Infrastructure stopped being present.<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. I've had a ton of fun running Demon so far, so I hope others really enjoy it as well. One of these days I'll get to play it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:13:19-08:00","id":17300,"title":"","content":"Seeing as Infrastructure isn't actually confined to the machine aesthetic... what if Compromise itself often completes an Occult Matrix required to slip angels in to tidy it up? Not just a mere signal to follow. A bit overly convenient, perhaps, but thematic in its own way. This still leaves room for a group in need of a massive Angelic Smitedown inspiring the building of special Infrastructure for that purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T19:59:42-08:00","id":17470,"title":"","content":"By the way, there'll be a section on angels in the Storyteller's Guide. Exiles, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}